<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>For each expression, write an equivalent expression in <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">standard form</term>. Show your reasoning.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\((2x+5)(x+1)\)</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para> \(2x^2+7x+5\). The diagram shows that\((2x+5)(x+1)=2x \cdot x+2x \cdot 1+5 \cdot x+5 \cdot 1\). Adding this
    together gives \(2x^2+7x+5\) in standard form.</para>
  <table>
    <tgroup cols="3"><thead>
      <row>
        <entry/>
        <entry>\(2x\)</entry>
        <entry>\(5\)</entry>
      </row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>\(x\)</entry>
        <entry>\(2x^2\)</entry>
        <entry>\(5x\)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>\(1\)</entry>
        <entry>\(2x\)</entry>
        <entry>\(5\)</entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </tgroup></table>
  </solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
    <problem>
      
      <para>\((x-2)(x+2)\)</para>
      <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(x^2-4\). \((x+2)(x-2)=x^2+(-2x)+2x+(-4)=x^2-4\).The diagram also shows that \((x+2)(x-2)=x^2-4\).</para>
    <table>
      <tgroup cols="3"><thead>
        <row>
          <entry/>
          <entry>\(x\)</entry>
          <entry>\(2\)</entry>
        </row>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry>\(x\)</entry>
          <entry>\(x^2\)</entry>
          <entry>\(2x\)</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>\(-2\)</entry>
          <entry>\(-2x\)</entry>
          <entry>\(-4\)</entry>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </tgroup></table></solution></exercise>
  </example></section>
</content>
